    "narrative": "The offensive anchor for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is undoubtedly **Corbin Carroll**, boasting a team-high efficiency score of 83.49. Despite the neutral park factors against Keller, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 10% boost for hitting at the top of the order and favorable SP matchup indicators, making him our premier asset for speed and run production. **James Wood** follows closely with a 76.28 score; while Scherzer remains a name of note, his 5.89 xERA signals a targetable matchup for **James Wood**, whose 0.420 xwOBA confirms he is in a prime position to capitalize on the volume of high-leverage plate appearances today. **Jose Caballero** also makes a compelling case as a strong start (76.02) despite hitting lower in the order, as the matchup against Schultz provides a significant 13% platoon boost that compensates for the lack of lineup protection.\n\nThe lineup construction was anchored by the necessity of stolen base potential, though we remain cautious with several active pieces. **Brice Turang** and **Isaac Paredes** occupy high-value spots pending lineup confirmation; **Brice Turang**\u2019s 69.36 score is bolstered by favorable wind conditions, while **Isaac Paredes** (67.28) is set to exploit a platoon advantage against Ure\u00f1a. On the bench, **Edwin Arroyo** pushed for consideration with a 50.60, but ultimately lacked the high-end scoring floor required to displace the utility or middle infield depth provided by **Jose Caballero** or **Zach McKinstry**. We are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley**; his 54.19 score is our lowest start, and with a 31% rain risk looming, he remains the most likely candidate to be pulled should the weather deteriorate or a high-upside replacement emerge from our reserves like **Travis Bazzana**. We continue to monitor **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** for health updates, while contributors like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Henry Bolte** remain available to rotate into the mix as the 2026 campaign progresses.",
